Source: creature-cm5-sensors
Section: kernel
Priority: optional
Maintainer: April White <april@opsnlops.io>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13), dh-sequence-dkms, device-tree-compiler
Standards-Version: 4.7.2
Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: creature-cm5-sensors
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, linux-headers-rpi-2712, raspi-firmware
Recommends: lm-sensors
Description: power and temperature sensors on the Creature CM5 Carrier board
 Makes the sensors on the Creature CM5 Carrier board visible through Linux
 hwmon, so sensors(1), /sys/class/hwmon and anything that reads hwmon can
 see them:
 .
  * PAC1954 four-channel power monitor (0x10 on I2C1): voltage, current and
    power for board input, the CM5 5 V rail, character power and PoE.
  * MCP9808 temperature sensor (0x18 on I2C1), using the in-kernel jc42
    driver.
 .
 The PAC1954 driver is built with DKMS, so it is rebuilt automatically for
 every new kernel. Installing the package installs the board's device tree
 overlay, enables it in /boot/firmware/config.txt and applies it straight
 away, so no reboot is needed.

Package: creature-cm5-audio
Section: sound
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, raspi-firmware
Recommends: alsa-utils
Description: audio outputs on the Creature CM5 Carrier board
 Enables the PCM5122 DAC behind the Creature CM5 Carrier board's RCA line
 output as the ALSA card "Creature Analog Audio" (hw:CreatureAnalog), and
 gives the HDMI port's card the ID CreatureDigital (hw:CreatureDigital).
 .
 The card is described in a device tree overlay using only generic kernel
 drivers (simple-audio-card, pcm512x and designware-i2s), so no out-of-tree
 module is needed. Installing the package installs the overlay and enables
 it in /boot/firmware/config.txt. If the Allo Boss DAC overlay was enabled
 for this DAC, it is commented out (and restored when this package is
 removed); switching from it takes effect at the next reboot.

Package: creature-cm5-revb-workarounds
Section: misc
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, i2c-tools, kmod
Description: workarounds for Creature CM5 Carrier rev B hardware bugs
 Install this only on rev B Creature CM5 Carrier boards. A systemd service
 runs at boot and works around known rev B hardware bugs:
 .
  * Character USB-C offers 5 V only. The TPS25750 PD controller can source
    only 5 V: its high-voltage power path is sink-only. The EEPROM still
    offers 12 V, so a sink that asks for 12 V loops through hard resets.
    The service rewrites the controller's source capabilities (in its RAM,
    not the EEPROM) to advertise 5 V / 3 A only.
 .
 The PD controller keeps the change until the board loses power. After the
 package is removed, the 12 V offer comes back at the next power cycle, and
 a sink that asks for 12 V loops through hard resets again.
